{"schema": "report-doc/1", "story": "tradeoff", "headline": "Cost and overall quality trade steadily: Brisk-S costs {cost_per_1k.brisk-s} per 1k conversations, Atlas-M {cost_per_1k.atlas-m}, Atlas-L {cost_per_1k.atlas-l}; the owner must price a point of quality.", "lede": "Nothing was declared in advance, so no option fails a gate and none can be called the winner. Each step up the cost frontier buys overall quality at a rising price per point; Open-70B is never the best buy.", "recommends": [], "confidence": {"form": "low", "caveats": [{"id": "nothing_declared", "material_if": "Any gate, floor or margin the owner declares later could remove an option, for example if Brisk-S's weak troubleshooting score were held to a floor."}, {"id": "no_control", "material_if": "A claim that one arm beats another is read from unpaired figures; it matters if a paired contrast would be narrower or wider than the unpaired interval."}, {"id": "best_of_n", "material_if": "Whichever option is picked from the four may read high by chance; it matters most if the pick leads the next option by little."}, {"id": "judge_unstated", "material_if": "Whose scores the judged figures are is unstated; it matters if the judge favours one arm's style, because the quality axis is all judged."}]}, "decision": [{"slot": "the_trade", "text": "Moving from Brisk-S to Atlas-M adds {price.brisk-s.atlas-m.overall.gain} points of overall quality for {price.brisk-s.atlas-m.overall.cost_gap} more per 1k conversations ({price.brisk-s.atlas-m.overall.per_point} per point). Moving on to Atlas-L adds {price.atlas-m.atlas-l.overall.gain} points for {price.atlas-m.atlas-l.overall.cost_gap} more ({price.atlas-m.atlas-l.overall.per_point} per point)."}, {"slot": "where_it_flips", "text": "Brisk-S is the best buy below {price.brisk-s.atlas-m.overall.per_point} per point, Atlas-M between {price.brisk-s.atlas-m.overall.per_point} and {price.atlas-m.atlas-l.overall.per_point}, Atlas-L above that. Open-70B is never best at any price."}, {"slot": "our_lean", "text": "Our lean, not a rule: Atlas-M, the middle step, unless the owner values quality above {price.atlas-m.atlas-l.overall.per_point} per point. Costs are this run's provider routing's, which the snapshot does not name."}, {"slot": "what_settles_it", "text": "The owner declares a price per quality point and any floor, for example on troubleshooting, where Brisk-S scores {task.trouble.brisk-s.overall.mean} against {task.trouble.atlas-l.overall.mean} for Atlas-L."}, {"slot": "watch", "text": "Brisk-S is weakest in troubleshooting ({task.trouble.brisk-s.overall.mean}) and research ({task.research.brisk-s.overall.mean}); the steps' gains carry only unpaired intervals."}], "claims": [{"id": "c1", "text": "Pooled overall quality rises with cost, and each step costs more per point than the last.", "weight": "lead", "evidence": [{"block": "table", "query": {"source": "prices", "aspect": "", "measures": ["overall"], "arms": [], "strata": [], "limit": 0, "transform": "none", "small_multiples_by": "none"}, "caption": "Price per point of overall quality at each step of the cost frontier; Open-70B is off the frontier."}]}, {"id": "c2", "text": "Brisk-S loses most on troubleshooting and research tasks, while Open-70B is close to the Atlas models only on persona small talk.", "weight": "support", "evidence": [{"block": "table", "query": {"source": "tasks", "aspect": "", "measures": ["overall"], "arms": [], "strata": [], "limit": 0, "transform": "none", "small_multiples_by": "none"}, "caption": "Overall quality by task and arm."}]}], "explore": [{"control": "Price per quality point", "binds": "Which option is the best buy", "outcome": "Below {price.brisk-s.atlas-m.overall.per_point} Brisk-S, up to {price.atlas-m.atlas-l.overall.per_point} Atlas-M, above that Atlas-L."}], "omitted": [{"what": "Per-aspect judged rates (resolves, steps, confirms and others)", "why": "Nothing declared which aspect matters; overall quality carries the trade. They stay in the full tables."}, {"what": "Latency", "why": "No latency budget was declared; the full table holds it."}, {"what": "A routed mix of models by task", "why": "Nobody ran it, so no figure prices it."}], "next": [{"text": "Run a routed mix that sends troubleshooting to Atlas-L and the rest to Brisk-S or Atlas-M, on the same cases.", "settles": "Whether most of the savings keep the quality where Brisk-S is weakest."}, {"text": "Declare a price per quality point and any task floor.", "settles": "Which option is the decision rather than a trade."}], "method": [{"term": "Quality", "text": "Overall quality is a judged rating pooled over tasks by traffic share; its judge is calibrated on {judged.overall.calibration_ratings} ratings with agreement {judged.overall.agreement}.", "caveats": ["judge_unstated"]}, {"term": "Cost basis", "text": "Cost per 1k conversations as served in this run; the provider routing is not named, so costs are not the models' own. No monthly volume is declared."}, {"term": "Intervals", "text": "Gain intervals are unpaired and descriptive; no control was declared."}]}
